    "interpretation": "The CGB identity requires 4\u03b4\u00b2Vol(conn) \u2265 12Vol(cusps) + (4/3)(3-\u03b4)\u00b2Vol(conn). For \u03b4 < 3(\u221a3-1)/2, the LHS 4\u03b4\u00b2 is too small to cover even the connector's own s\u00b2 integral, regardless of cusp volume. The floor is sharp at \u03b4 = 3(\u221a3-1)/2 \u2248 1.098 when |W|=0 and all volumes balance. This means even the connector ALONE (as part of a closed \u03c7=0 manifold) cannot have operator-norm defect below 1.098."
